MLLM description: The wire-haired fox terrier is a small to medium-sized dog with a distinctive, wiry coat that is dense, short, and close-lying. Its head is elongated with a slightly arched skull, a long muzzle, and a black nose. The ears are small, triangular, and set high on the head, often folded over at the tips. The tail is long, bushy, and carried high.

In terms of color patterns and markings, the wire-haired fox terrier can come in various combinations of white and black, with some dogs having a predominantly white coat with black markings, while others may have a predominantly black coat with white markings. The most common pattern is a "broken" or "parti-color" coat, where the body is predominantly white with large black patches.

The size and proportions of the wire-haired fox terrier are compact and well-proportioned, with a sturdy build and a level topline. They stand alert and confident, exuding energy and intelligence.

