MLLM description: Giant pandas are easily recognizable by their distinctive black-and-white coloration, which is unique to this species. Their fur is primarily white with large black patches around the eyes, ears, and limbs. The black markings create a striking contrast against the white fur, making them stand out visually.

Physically, giant pandas have a robust build, with a thick layer of fur that provides insulation in their native cold habitats. They possess a stocky body, short legs, and a relatively small head compared to their body size. Their face is round, with a flat snout and small, rounded ears. Giant pandas also have a characteristic hump on their shoulders, which houses their powerful muscles used for their strong grip on bamboo.

Behaviorally, giant pandas are known for their slow and deliberate movements, often seen lounging or eating bamboo. They are primarily solitary animals, except during mating season, and are excellent climbers, using their long, curved claws to grasp branches and stems.

The unique identifying traits of giant pandas include their black-and-white coloration, round face, and hump on their shoulders. These features, combined with their specific habitat requirements and diet, make them distinct from other bear species.
